        {
            "Section": "DS_TIG_DISP.DSDECOD",
            "Unnamed: 1": "DSDECOD",
            "Unnamed: 2": "What was the subject's status?",
            "Unnamed: 3": "text",
            "Unnamed: 4": 3,
            "Unnamed: 5": "No",
            "Unnamed: 6": "T_11",
            "Unnamed: 7": 8,
            "Unnamed: 8": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 9": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 10": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 11": "DSDECOD [CDASH]\nDSDECOD [SDTM]\nDocument the subject's status for the study or study period. If the subject discontinued prematurely, record the primary reason for discontinuation. [completionInstructions]\nDSDECOD can be used as the standardized coded list with DSTERM used to capture any \"Specify, Other\" information, or DSDECOD can be used on its own. For Sponsor- and/or study-specific reasons for discontinuation, it is recommended that these reasons be preprinted on the CRF, as subcategories of the appropriate standardized DSDECOD item. However, it is recommended to limit the use of sponsor and study-specific reasons in order to promote consistent use of terminology and hence permit the combination of data across multiple sponsors. Either DSTERM or DSDECOD must be on the CRF. Both may be used if DSTERM is used as a \"Specify, Other\" field.   [implementationNotes]\nStatus [prompt]",
            "Unnamed: 12": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 13": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 14": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 15": "DSDECODE",
            "Unnamed: 16": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 17": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 18": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 19": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 20": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 21": NaN
        },
        {
            "Section": "DS_TIG_DISP.DSTERM",
            "Unnamed: 1": "DSTERM",
            "Unnamed: 2": "What was the verbatim reason for the subject status?",
            "Unnamed: 3": "text",
            "Unnamed: 4": 4,
            "Unnamed: 5": "No",
            "Unnamed: 6": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 7": 8,
            "Unnamed: 8": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 9": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 10": "DSTERM [en]",
            "Unnamed: 11": "DSTERM [CDASH]\nDSTERM [SDTM]\nIf Adverse Experiences, Death, Protocol Deviation or Other is selected from the Status list, provide the verbatim reason. [completionInstructions]\nFree text verbatim description of the subject's status. This field would only be used in conjunction with DSDECOD. Allows details to be collected about the subject status. [implementationNotes]\nMaps directly to the SDTMIG variable listed in the column with the heading SDTMIG Target. The SDTMIG variables DSDECOD and DSTERM must be populated in SDTM. If DSTERM was collected as an \"Other, Specify\" free text, populate the SDTMIG variable DSTERM with the free text and populate DSDECOD with the sponsor-defined standardized text. If DSDECOD was collected with no free text, populate DSTERM and DSDECOD in the SDTM-based dataset with the DSDECOD value that was collected. [mappingInstructions]\nSpecify [prompt]",
            "Unnamed: 12": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 13": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 14": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 15": "DSTERM",
            "Unnamed: 16": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 17": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 18": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 19": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 20": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 21": NaN
        },
        {
            "Section": "DS_TIG_DISP.DSSTDAT",
            "Unnamed: 1": "DSSTDAT",
            "Unnamed: 2": "What was the completion/discontinuation date?",
            "Unnamed: 3": "date",
            "Unnamed: 4": 5,
            "Unnamed: 5": "No",
            "Unnamed: 6": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 7": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 8": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 9": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 10": "DSSTDAT [en]",
            "Unnamed: 11": "DSSTDAT [CDASH]\nDSSTDTC [SDTM]\nRecord the date that the subject completed the study or study period\u00a0 using this format. If the subject did not complete the study or study period, record the date that the subject discontinued. [completionInstructions]\nDefine in the protocol and/or CRF completion instructions the criteria for completion of each protocol milestone or disposition event for which a disposition CRF will be provided. Only collect the date of each protocol milestone or disposition event once. For example, if the date of the last dose is defined to mark the end of the Treatment Phase epoch, and is collected on the Exposure form, then this field would not be collected on the Disposition CRF module. If not collected elsewhere, this field should be collected on the Disposition CRF module. [implementationNotes]\nDisposition Date [prompt]",
            "Unnamed: 12": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 13": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 14": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 15": "DSSTDTC",
